{
  "dom_id": "question-79877",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14215763/assets/49b119b378ac4f45c0c395ca77c5cefead3a7c811295b51ac8eaa8aef7100e25.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curves $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and $y=-1,$  as shown in the picture. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are rectangles. If the height of each rectangle is $2$ times the length of its base, which integral gives the volume of the solid?",
